# Keep the build context lean. The multi-stage Dockerfile builds OpenMW FROM SOURCE (needs openmw/,
# fsroot/, wasm-build/, configure-openmw.sh) inside the prebaked builder image, then serves play/
# statics via caddy. So exclude vcs, the dep tree (baked into openmw-builder), build outputs, and the
# large prebuilt/game binaries — none of which belong in the context.
.git
.github
openmw/.git-upstream
deps
build-wasm
archive
source-mw
content
node_modules
infra
**/*.bak
**/*.simd.bak
# play/: keep only the tracked static web files; the engine artifacts come from the builder stage,
# and game data / brotli blobs are shipped/mounted separately.
play/openmw.wasm
play/openmw.data
play/openmw.js.br
play/openmw.wasm.br
play/openmw.data.br
play/mwdata
play/*.tar
*.7z
*.zip
.DS_Store
# wasm-build/ is COPYed into the builder stage BEFORE the 25-min engine compile, and BuildKit keys
# that layer on the whole directory -- so editing a test-only file here forced a full engine
# rebuild + brotli on the VPS (35 min, measured 2026-09-04). The build reads only the .sh/.py
# scripts, include/, patches/, x11_stubs.c and the memory64/f10 gates; none of these.
wasm-build/mp-harness.mjs
wasm-build/mp-scenarios
wasm-build/lua-tests
wasm-build/mp-vectors.mjs
wasm-build/qa.mjs
wasm-build/qa2.mjs
wasm-build/smoke.mjs
wasm-build/p3.mjs
wasm-build/perf-ab.mjs
wasm-build/selftest.mjs
wasm-build/memory64-gate-browser.mjs
wasm-build/memory64-gate-run.mjs
wasm-build/Dockerfile.harness
wasm-build/Dockerfile.harness-peer
